    "Description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: scsi: core: Wake up the error handler when final completions race against each other (CVE-2026-23110)\n\n* kernel: net: atm: fix crash due to unvalidated vcc pointer in sigd_send() (CVE-2026-31411)\n\n* kernel: crypto: ccp - copy IV using skcipher ivsize (CVE-2026-53016)\n\n* kernel: dm log: fix out-of-bounds write due to region_count overflow (CVE-2026-53059)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* Kernels 5.14.0-434+ may lose page table dirty bit (and page data) [rhel-9.6.z] (JIRA:RHEL-220786)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
